# 001
JPSupport-Qt: Qt6 widgetset bindings only (QInputMethodEvent attributes + LCL slots)

Against: Lazarus fixes_4 (generated from 4cab00d2, 2026-09-27)
Apply:   git apply jpsupport-qt-qt6-bindings.patch   (or: patch -p1 < ...)

Files:
  lcl/interfaces/qt6/cbindings/src/qevent_c.h / qevent_c.cpp
      New C accessors for QInputMethodEvent::attributes() (count / type /
      start / length / backgroundColor / bold). Read-only wrappers; no
      existing exported symbol is changed. Needs libQt6Pas rebuilt.
  lcl/interfaces/qt6/qt62.pas
      Pascal external declarations for the accessors above.
  lcl/interfaces/qt6/qtwidgets.pas
      TQtWidget.SlotInputMethod: forwards preedit text + segments/cursor
      to the LCL control via LM_IM_SET_PREEDIT; fixes truncation of
      multi-character commit strings (UTF-16 WideString was decoded as
      UTF-8). New TQtWidget.SlotInputMethodQuery answers
      Qt::ImCursorRectangle via LM_IM_QUERY_CARET_POS.

NOT included (shared with the Qt5 widgetset, see the other patch):
  lcl/lmessages.pp  - defines LM_IM_QUERY_CARET_POS, LM_IM_SET_PREEDIT,
                      TIMEPreeditInfo. qtwidgets.pas above will not
                      compile without it.
  components/synedit/* - the consumer side (LazSynIme / LazSynImeQt).
Controls that do not handle these messages (TEdit/QLineEdit) leave
Msg.Result = 0 and keep the previous native Qt behaviour.

